Rem ==================================================================
Rem seedregex.shoddy — reckoner seed: regex.shoddy at the keyboard
Rem
Rem RXTEST, RXFIND, RXFINDALL, RXGROUPS, RXREPLACE, RXSPLIT, RXQUOTE and
Rem RXWHY. Eight words, all pure, so a calculator can ask a stated rule
Rem about a string it is holding:
Rem
Rem     "GET 200 /index.html" "^(\w+) (\d+)" RXGROUPS
Rem     "a, b,,c" ",\s*" RXSPLIT
Rem     "2026-08-08" "^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$" RXTEST
Rem
Rem THE PATTERN IS A STRING AND IS COMPILED ON EVERY CALL. That is a
Rem deliberate cost and not an oversight. A compiled program is a
Rem machine type, and Cell in cuttle.shoddy has eight kinds of which
Rem none is one: adding a ninth would change the file every seed
Rem includes, and would need a text form for the tape, an equality and a
Rem rendering for a value that has none of those naturally. Against that,
Rem A LINE IS TYPED BY A PERSON — the pattern is a dozen characters and
Rem the compile is microseconds against a keystroke. Where a program
Rem wants the pattern compiled once, it uses RxRead and the machine
Rem directly; that is what the machine is for.
Rem
Rem WHAT THE BRIDGE LOSES, SAID OUT LOUD. RXGROUPS answers a LIST of
Rem STRINGs, so A GROUP THAT DID NOT PARTICIPATE ARRIVES AS "" — exactly
Rem the distinction regex.shoddy is built to preserve, flattened by the
Rem Cell type on the way to the stack. (a)|(b) against "b" gives
Rem { "b", "", "b" } and nothing in that list says which "" is a group
Rem that matched nothing and which is a group that was never entered.
Rem RxGroup is where the distinction still lives, and a program that
Rem needs it must go to the machine. A BRIDGE THAT QUIETLY FLATTENS A
Rem TYPE IS THE THING WORTH WRITING DOWN.
Rem
Rem RxReplaceWith is NOT seeded: it takes a quotation per hit and a Cell
Rem cannot carry one. Running a user-defined reckoner word per match is
Rem a real idea and its own proposal — it needs a seed to call back into
Rem RckEval mid-word, which no seed does today.
Rem
Rem GUARDED BY CONSTRUCTION. regex.shoddy has not one call to Error in
Rem it: RxRead answers the language's Result and every match word takes
Rem a compiled program, which can only have come from an Ok. So there is
Rem no aborting path into the machine from anywhere, and this seed does
Rem not have to find one and avoid it. Every guard below is therefore
Rem about the SHAPE OF THE STACK — a cell that is not a STRING — plus
Rem one Select Case over RxRead, and that is the whole of it.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "regex.shoddy"
Include "cuttle.shoddy"
Include "reckoner.shoddy"

Rem ---- the guards, written once ---------------------------------------
Rem Six of the eight words are ( s pat -- ... ), so their whole guard is
Rem one chain: the subject is a STRING, the pattern is a STRING, and the
Rem pattern reads. What is left after that is a subject and a compiled
Rem program, and nothing that can be wrong.

Def RgWith(word As String, vs As List Of Cell, f As [ String RxProg -- RckWork ]) As RckWork
    Select Case RckTextArg(word, Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(s)
            RgWith2(word, s, Nth(vs, 2), f)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(word & " did not answer")

Def RgWith2(word As String, s As String, c As Cell, f As [ String RxProg -- RckWork ]) As RckWork
    Select Case RckTextArg(word, c)
        Case Ok(pat)
            RgWith3(word, s, pat, f)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(word & " did not answer")

Def RgWith3(word As String, s As String, pat As String, f As [ String RxProg -- RckWork ]) As RckWork
    Select Case RxRead(pat, RxNoOpts())
        Case Ok(prg)
            Call(f, s, prg)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(RgWhyAt(w, at))
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(word & " did not answer")

Rem The refusal a person sees is the machine's reason and the place in
Rem the pattern it was written, which is the only thing that turns a
Rem mistyped pattern into a fixed one.
Def RgWhyAt(w As String, at As Number) As String
    If at = 0 Then
        w
    Else
        w & " (at " & Str(at) & ")"

Rem ---- RXTEST ---------------------------------------------------------

Def RgSeedTest(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "RXTEST", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => RgWith("RXTEST", vs, RgTestGo)), "( s pat -- flag )", "Whether pat matches anywhere in s.")

Def RgTestGo(s As String, prg As RxProg) As RckWork
    RckVals({ CutBool(RxTest(prg, s)) })

Rem ---- RXFIND ---------------------------------------------------------
Rem TWO CELLS, ALWAYS, and 0 0 where there is no match. A word that
Rem pushed a variable number of cells would break UNDO's accounting, so
Rem the miss is a pair of zeros rather than nothing — and 0 is a start
Rem no real match can have, since the subject is 1-based.

Def RgSeedFind(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "RXFIND", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => RgWith("RXFIND", vs, RgFindGo)), "( s pat -- at len )", "The leftmost match's 1-based start and its length; 0 0 when there is none.")

Def RgFindGo(s As String, prg As RxProg) As RckWork
    Select Case RxFind(prg, s)
        Case Some(h)
            RckVals({ CutNum(RxHitAt(h)), CutNum(RxHitLen(h)) })
        Case Else
            RckVals({ CutNum(0), CutNum(0) })

Rem ---- RXFINDALL ------------------------------------------------------

Def RgSeedFindAll(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "RXFINDALL", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => RgWith("RXFINDALL", vs, RgFindAllGo)), "( s pat -- list )", "Every non-overlapping match, in order, as a LIST of STRINGs.")

Def RgFindAllGo(s As String, prg As RxProg) As RckWork
    RckVals({ CutList(Map(RxFindAll(prg, s), RgHitCell)) })

Def RgHitCell(h As RxHit) As Cell
    CutStr(RxHitText(h))

Rem ---- RXGROUPS -------------------------------------------------------
Rem The first match only: the whole match, then one item per capturing
Rem group, in group order. An unset group arrives as "" — see the header.

Def RgSeedGroups(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "RXGROUPS", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => RgWith("RXGROUPS", vs, RgGroupsGo)), "( s pat -- list )", "The first match as a LIST: the whole match, then one item per group. An unset group arrives as an empty string.")

Def RgGroupsGo(s As String, prg As RxProg) As RckWork
    Select Case RxFind(prg, s)
        Case Some(h)
            RckVals({ CutList(Prepend(CutStr(RxHitText(h)), RgCapsOf(h, RxCount(prg), 1, { }))) })
        Case Else
            RckVals({ CutList({ }) })

Def RgCapsOf(h As RxHit, ncap As Number, gn As Number, acc As List Of Cell) As List Of Cell
    If gn > ncap Then
        Reverse(acc)
    Else
        RgCapsOf(h, ncap, gn + 1, Prepend(CutStr(RxGroupOr(h, gn, "")), acc))

Rem ---- RXREPLACE ------------------------------------------------------
Rem Three strings, so this one guards its own stack rather than sharing
Rem the pair guard above.

Def RgSeedReplace(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "RXREPLACE", 3, RckPure(Fn(vs) => RgReplace(vs)), "( s pat rep -- s )", "Every match of pat in s replaced by rep, where $0 to $9 stand for the match and its groups and $$ is a literal dollar.")

Def RgReplace(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckTextArg("RXREPLACE", Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(s)
            RgReplace2(s, Nth(vs, 2), Nth(vs, 3))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("RXREPLACE did not answer")

Def RgReplace2(s As String, cpat As Cell, crep As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckTextArg("RXREPLACE", cpat)
        Case Ok(pat)
            RgReplace3(s, pat, crep)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("RXREPLACE did not answer")

Def RgReplace3(s As String, pat As String, crep As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckTextArg("RXREPLACE", crep)
        Case Ok(rep)
            RgReplace4(s, pat, rep)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("RXREPLACE did not answer")

Def RgReplace4(s As String, pat As String, rep As String) As RckWork
    Select Case RxRead(pat, RxNoOpts())
        Case Ok(prg)
            RckVals({ CutStr(RxReplace(prg, s, rep)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(RgWhyAt(w, at))
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("RXREPLACE did not answer")

Rem ---- RXSPLIT --------------------------------------------------------

Def RgSeedSplit(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "RXSPLIT", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => RgWith("RXSPLIT", vs, RgSplitGo)), "( s pat -- list )", "s cut apart at every match of pat, as a LIST of STRINGs, leading and trailing empty pieces kept.")

Def RgSplitGo(s As String, prg As RxProg) As RckWork
    RckVals({ CutList(Map(RxSplit(prg, s), CutStr)) })

Rem ---- RXQUOTE --------------------------------------------------------
Rem One string, and nothing that can fail: every string has an escaping.

Def RgSeedQuote(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "RXQUOTE", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => RgQuote(vs)), "( s -- pat )", "s escaped so that, used as a pattern, it matches itself and nothing else.")

Def RgQuote(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckTextArg("RXQUOTE", First(vs))
        Case Ok(s)
            RckVals({ CutStr(RxQuote(s)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("RXQUOTE did not answer")

Rem ---- RXWHY ----------------------------------------------------------
Rem The one word here that is about the pattern rather than about a
Rem subject: it answers "" when the pattern reads, and the reason with
Rem its offset when it does not. It is how a person finds out what is
Rem wrong with a pattern WITHOUT having to have a subject to try it on.

Def RgSeedWhy(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "RXWHY", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => RgWhy(vs)), "( pat -- s )", "An empty string if pat reads; otherwise why it does not, and where.")

Def RgWhy(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckTextArg("RXWHY", First(vs))
        Case Ok(pat)
            RgWhyOf(pat)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("RXWHY did not answer")

Def RgWhyOf(pat As String) As RckWork
    Select Case RxRead(pat, RxNoOpts())
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckVals({ CutStr(RgWhyAt(w, at)) })
        Case Else
            RckVals({ CutStr("") })

Rem ---- the seed -------------------------------------------------------

Def RckSeedRegex(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s0 = RckSeeding(st, "seed-regex")
    Let s1 = RgSeedTest(s0)
    Let s2 = RgSeedFind(s1)
    Let s3 = RgSeedFindAll(s2)
    Let s4 = RgSeedGroups(s3)
    Let s5 = RgSeedReplace(s4)
    Let s6 = RgSeedSplit(s5)
    Let s7 = RgSeedQuote(s6)
    RgSeedWhy(s7)
